{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027744-the-mechanics-of-a-combination-spell","id":1027744,"title":"The mechanics of a Combination spell.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-06T10:20:00-08:00","id":1027744,"title":"The mechanics of a Combination spell.","content":"Here I am with another question about how to do something. As i have stated i have been playing a little more than a month so there are some aspects of the game that are a little harder to figure out.<br /> <br /> I want to Cast 2 spells, Both spells are from the Life Arcanum (Heighten Senses and Transform Life). I have a gnosis of 3 and life 3 (Common Arcanum).<br /> <br /> <b>Transform Life (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina<br /> <br /> <b>Heightened Senses (Life \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unveiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <br /> <b>Spell Factors:</b> Which spell factors are used in the combo spell?<br /> <br /> <b>Primary spell factor:</b> What is the primary spell factor for the combined spell? Is it Potency (from Transform Life) or Duration (from Heightened Senses)? Do they each retain their own primary spell factor and the duration and potency will be different for each spell? Would it cost a reach to change the Primary spell factor of Heightened senses from Duration to potency.<br /> <br /> <b>Free Reach:</b> Is the free reaches figure from the Transform Life (1 free reach) or from the Heightened Senses (3 free reaches). Or do they each have the free reaches that are normal for the spell and i would apply them separately?<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> 3 (Gnosis) +3(Life) -2 (Combo spell). If I increase the Duration by step 1 by taking a -2 dice pool, Does that affect the entire spell or do I need to take a -2 for each spell in the combo to increase that factor? My understanding is that it affects both spells and I would have to take a reach to let it only affect 1 of the spells.<br /> <br /> <b>Withstand:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> If one has withstand the other doesn't, and subject withstands it are both spell nullified?</span></span><br /> <br /> If someone could explain the process it would be greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-06-2017, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T11:11:54-08:00","id":1027763,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that while the casting action happens a single time, the spell effects remain separate and are considered separately.<br /> <br /> Primary Spell Factor: My understanding is that if you don't modify the Potency or Duration, then your Transform Life would last a turn and have Potency 3 and the Heightened Senses would last 3 turns and have Potency 1.<br /> <br /> Free Reach: I would expect you to only get 1 free Reach, because otherwise it seems like a cheap exploit to take a -2 in return for a bunch of free Reaches. (Likewise, I'd expect to get zero free Reaches when casting at the limit of my ability in 2+ Arcana.)<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: I would agree with your understanding: it affects the entire pool, so taking -2 for extra Duration would make Transform Life last 2 turns and Heightened Senses last 5 turns.<br /> <br /> Withstand: Withstanding a spell doesn't nullify it; it reduces the Potency. So assuming again that we're not touching spell factors, if Transform Life is Withstood by Stamina 3 and Heightened Senses is not Withstood, then Transform Life would have no effect (Potency 0) but Heightened Senses would be fine (Potency 1).<br /> <br /> So, based on this, my rule of thumb would be: If it's considered before you roll dice, combine it; if it's considered after you roll dice, separate it. So the number of times you apply a spell factor happens before you roll dice, because that's just determining dice penalty. But the actual effects of that application come <i>afterwards</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T12:05:10-08:00","id":1027785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027744-the-mechanics-of-a-combination-spell?p=1027763#post1027763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primary Spell Factor: My understanding is that if you don't modify the Potency or Duration, then your Transform Life would last a turn and have Potency 3 and the Heightened Senses would last 3 turns and have Potency 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Combined spells explicitly share spell factors, so while I'm not sure what the correct answer is, this doesn't seem to be it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T14:01:23-08:00","id":1027841,"title":"","content":"I see that others are as confused about this as I am.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T14:40:27-08:00","id":1027853,"title":"","content":"After just reading it over, noticed a few things.<br /> <br /> Spell factors and Yantras affect all spells equally. This leads me to believe that extends to the Primary Spell Factors, so in you're above example both spells would have Potency and Duration at 3 to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11839-cofdave","name":"CofDave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T02:05:13-08:00","id":1028072,"title":"","content":"So, I'm going to list the way our group runs it, with the bolded parts being things that are explicitly stated in the book:<ul><li>If combining spells with multiple primary factors, both factors gain the free steps (<b>because the combined spell shares spell factors</b>).</li> <li>Free Reach is calculated based off of the lowest available free reach of the component spells. (An alternative option is that free reach is calculated for each component individually.)</li> <li><b>Reach that effects spell factors applies to the whole combined spell</b>.</li> <li><b>Reach that does not effect spell factors is applied to a component spell</b>.</li> <li><b>Dice Pool is based off of the lowest Arcanum used in the component spells</b>.</li> <li><b>Component spells are Withstood separately</b>.</li> </ul>Now I'm going to include a sample combined spell from one of our games. This is an Archmaster's spell, cast using six soul stones as Yantras, so not really a common example but it's the only one I have at hand to include. The subject mage has 10 Gnosis, 6 Time, 4 Space, and 4 Prime. Only one of the component spells has extra reach effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Note that we're playing with rules that allow Archmasters to cast using advanced spell factors without reaching for them. Were that not the case, there would need to be one additional reach for Advanced Duration (applying to the whole spell) for the same effects</b>:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cloak of the Moon </span></span><span style=\"color:#CC0000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Cloak Nimbus</span></span><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><sup><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1</span></sup></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, Ward</span></span><sup><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2</span></span></sup><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, </span></span><span style=\"color:#3C78D8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Constant Presence</span></span><sup><span style=\"color:#3C78D8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3</span></span></sup><span style=\"color:#3C78D8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, Shield of Chronos</span></span><sup><span style=\"color:#3C78D8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4</span></span></sup><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">) </span></span><span style=\"color:#9900FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Oneiros]</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Ritual</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- 6 Minutes (+5)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chains</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - The Moon (+2), Justice (+2), Death (+2), The Sun (+2), The Fool (+2), The Devil (+2)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 Free Reach</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Lesser Time</span></span><sup><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1</span></span></sup><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, Lesser Mana</span></span><sup><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1</span></span></sup><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, Lesser Gnosis</span></span><sup><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1</span></span></sup><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 Overreach</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Lesser Fate</span></span><sup><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1</span></span></sup><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, Lesser Space</span></span><sup><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1</span></span></sup><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, Lesser Prime</span></span><sup><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">1</span></span></sup><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Spell Factor</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Potency &amp; Duration +4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This spell grants the following effects to the subject for one year.</span></span><ul><li>The subject\u2019s true level of power is hidden. Any form of Aura Reading, including Supernal Vision, provokes a Clash of Wills. If the caster succeeds, the subject appears to have 4 dots of Gnosis, 13 Mana, 4 dots in Time, 3 dots in Fate, 2 Dots in Space, and 1 dot in Prime. In addition, while under the effect of this spell, her signature nimbus is muted, and her Immediate Nimbus does not flare when casting.</li> <li>The subject\u2019s sympathetic connections are warded. Magic using the sympathy of the subject provokes a Clash of Wills.</li> <li>The subject is preserved against alterations to the timeline. Any alteration to history through the action of time travel provokes a Clash of Wills. If the mage wins, the subject is treated as though she was also a returning time traveller when history resettles.</li> <li>The subject is shielded against temporal senses. Attempts to view the subject through time provoke a Clash of Wills.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- 24 (Gnosis 10, Space 4, Ritual 5, Chains 12, Combined Spell -6)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spell Control</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - No Penalty</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Paradox</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Chance Die (1 Elder Diadem, 15 Reach, Oneiros)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Releasing / Containing / Controlling</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Controlling</span></span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-07-2017, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T04:22:59-08:00","id":1028110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027744-the-mechanics-of-a-combination-spell?p=1028072#post1028072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm going to list the way our group runs it, with the bolded parts being things that are explicitly stated in the book:<ul><li>If combining spells with multiple primary factors, both factors gain the free steps (<b>because the combined spell shares spell factors</b>).</li> <li>Free Reach is calculated based off of the lowest available free reach of the component spells. (An alternative option is that free reach is calculated for each component individually.)</li> <li><b>Reach that effects spell factors applies to the whole combined spell</b>.</li> <li><b>Reach that does not effect spell factors is applied to a component spell</b>.</li> <li><b>Dice Pool is based off of the lowest Arcanum used in the component spells</b>.</li> <li><b>Component spells are Withstood separately</b>.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I Do not see anything that mentions Primary Spell Factors.<ol class=\"lower-alpha\"><li>I do see where it states that Spell modifications from Yantras and spell factors affect the entire spell, but I believe that they are referring to the spell modifications that are derived from taking a negative to the dice pool.</li> <li>I do agree that they share spell factors and that a primary spell factor need to be determined in some manor.</li> </ol></li> <li>I see this and I agree.<ol class=\"lower-alpha\"><li>I don't agree with the optional part but an argument could be made that supports this view.</li> </ol></li> <li>I see this and I agree.</li> <li>I see this and I agree.</li> <li>I see this and I agree, with a -2 per spell combined over the first, and then all negatives from spell factors.</li> <li>I don't see where withstand is mentioned at all in the section that talks about combination spells.<ol class=\"lower-alpha\"><li>I do not agree with your interpretation but an argument could be made that supports this view.</li> </ol></li> </ol>If it was me I would run it like this.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Primary spell factor: </b>If the combined spells have different spell factors that the mage chooses the primary spell factor.</li> <li><b>Free Reach:</b> Free reach is calculated normally for each spell involved and then you take the lowest number, that is the number of free reaches available.</li> <li><b>Dice Pool: </b>The entire spell has one dice pool and it is figured as follows. Gnosis + Lowest Arcanum -2 for each spell after the first - spell factor adjustments that affect the entire spell.</li> <li><b>Withstand: </b>If different withstands then the mage chooses.<ol class=\"lower-alpha\"><li>if 1 spell has a withstand and the other(s) do not then the withstand is applied to the entire spell removing potency from all components of the combined spell.</li> <li>As mentioned above I could be convinced to allow withstand to affect each component of the spell separately.</li> </ol></li> <li><b>Scale:</b> The entire spell is the same unless a reach is used to have a different scale for each component.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-07-2017, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T04:37:23-08:00","id":1028113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027744-the-mechanics-of-a-combination-spell?p=1028110#post1028110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see where withstand is mentioned at all in the section that talks about combination spells<br /> I do not agree with your interpretation but an argument could be made that supports this view.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not listed in the correct section, but it is explicitly stated, so it's not an interpretation and no argument is to be made. M2E p114, under the section 'Withstanding'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each spell in a combined spell is Withstood separately. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T06:01:28-08:00","id":1028126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027744-the-mechanics-of-a-combination-spell?p=1028113#post1028113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not listed in the correct section, but it is explicitly stated, so it's not an interpretation and no argument is to be made. M2E p114, under the section 'Withstanding'.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the page number and I see that now. As mentioned I could see that and could be convinced to it's merits. But now no convincing is needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-07-2017, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T07:47:57-08:00","id":1028146,"title":"","content":"This is how it is going to be handled in the game I will be running.<br /> <br /> Your Gnosis will determined the number of spells that can be combined into one casting. It is two at Gnosis 3, three at Gnosis 6, and four at Gnosis 9.<br /> <br /> You may not have a rote in your combined spell.<br /> <br /> You may combine Praxis spells if all spells involved are Praxis spells.<br /> <br /> The following is the Spell Factors for the spell:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> If the combined spells have different spell factors then the mage chooses the primary spell factor. That becomes the Primary Spell Factor for all component spells of the combination.</li> <li><b>Free Reach:</b> Free reach is calculated normally for each spell involved and then you take the lowest number, that is the number of free reaches available.<br /> The use of a reach<ol class=\"lower-alpha\"><li>When using a reach it affects all component spells of the combination.</li> <li>Spell specific reaches can be purchased on a per spell basis and affect only the spell they were purchased for.</li> </ol></li> <li><b>Dice Pool:</b> The entire spell has one dice pool and it is figured as follows. Gnosis + Lowest Arcanum + Yantras + willpower (if used) -2 for each spell after the first - Spell Factor modifications.<br /> Dice Pool modifications<ol class=\"lower-alpha\"><li>Yantras affect the dice pool as normal. If using a Yantra it must be relevant to all component spells of the combination.</li> <li>If you take a negative to modify a spell factor it modifies that spell factor for all component spells of the combination.</li> </ol></li> <li><b>Withstand:</b> Each spell in a combined spell is Withstood separately. If a spell has multiple Withstand ratings (for example, a Withstood spell cast with the Sympathetic Range Attainment) it uses the highest rating, +1 for every additional rating.</li> <li><b>Scale:</b> Multiple spell effects must use the same scale unless the mage uses a Reach to separate the effects.</li> <li><b>Potency:</b> Is figured the same a normal, increasing the spell factor with either a reach or by taking a negative to the dice pool. This affects the Potency for all component spells of the combination.</li> <li><b>Duration:</b> Is figured the same a normal, increasing the spell factor with either a reach or by taking a negative to the dice pool. This affects the Duration for all component spells of the combination.</li> <li><b>Range:</b> Is figured the same a normal, increasing the spell factor with either a reach or by taking a negative to the dice pool. This affects the Range for all component spells of the combination.</li> <li><b>Casting Time:</b> Casting time is unchanged and the entire combined spell uses your Gnosis derived casting time for a ritual or if you spend a reach to make it an instant spell then the entire spell is an instant.</li> <li><b>Mana:</b> You must include all mana needed for each component spell used in the combination.</li> <li><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Since a combined spell cannot have a rote in it this doesn't come into play.</li> </ol>As an Example: You have Gnosis 6, Fate 4, Life 3 and Death 2. If combining Touch of the Grave (Death \u2022\u2022), Grave Misfortune (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022) and Transform Life (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022) it would look like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Spell Factor:</b> The mage would choose this, smart thing would to choose Potency.<br /> <b>Free Reach:</b> 1 free reach (2 free reach from Fate, 1 free reach from Life and 1 free reach from Death, take the lowest one)<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Gnosis 6 + 2 (Death) - 4 combining 3 spells, +/- Yantras, Willpower and Spell factor modifications.<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Touch of the Grave is not withstood, Grave Misfortune is withstood by Composure and Transform Life is withstood by Stamina.<br /> <b>Scale:</b> The scale for all components is 1 person unless modified.<br /> <b>Potency:</b> The Potency for all components is 1 unless modified.<br /> <b>Duration:</b> The Duration for all components is 1 round unless modified.<br /> <b>Range:</b> The Range for all components is touch unless modified.<br /> <b>Casting Time:</b> The Casting Time for all components is 1 round (plus Yantras used -1) unless modified.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Touch of the Grave (Death \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Ruling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <br /> <b>Grave Misfortune (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Composure<br /> <br /> <b>Transform Life (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Stamina","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-07-2017, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T18:44:25-08:00","id":1028369,"title":"","content":"I'd avoid giving the Mage the chance to choose Primary Spell Factor. It opens up a very exploitable loop hole to just combi-cast a same or lower dot spell in order to get a free change in Primary Factor instead of the Reach that is required.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T01:34:04-08:00","id":1028465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027744-the-mechanics-of-a-combination-spell?p=1028369#post1028369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd avoid giving the Mage the chance to choose Primary Spell Factor. It opens up a very exploitable loop hole to just combi-cast a same or lower dot spell in order to get a free change in Primary Factor instead of the Reach that is required.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unfortunately I don't see in the book a different way. Until presented with a better way or the Devs chime in I think I will leave it as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T02:52:49-08:00","id":1028472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027744-the-mechanics-of-a-combination-spell?p=1028369#post1028369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd avoid giving the Mage the chance to choose Primary Spell Factor. It opens up a very exploitable loop hole to just combi-cast a same or lower dot spell in order to get a free change in Primary Factor instead of the Reach that is required.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would you suggest for an alternative? The only real options are<br /> 1) Both get free steps (what my group uses)<br /> 2) Caster chooses which gets free steps (Hardwire's method)<br /> 3) You can only combine spells with the same primary factor (a severe restriction, if this was RAI I would expect that to be called out somewhere)<br /> 4) You don't get any free steps at all (a severe restriction, if this was RAI I would expect that to be called out somewhere)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T03:02:31-08:00","id":1028475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027744-the-mechanics-of-a-combination-spell?p=1028472#post1028472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you suggest for an alternative? The only real options are<br /> 1) Both get free steps (what my group uses)<br /> 2) Caster chooses which gets free steps (Hardwire's method)<br /> 3) You can only combine spells with the same primary factor (a severe restriction, if this was RAI I would expect that to be called out somewhere)<br /> 4) You don't get any free steps at all (a severe restriction, if this was RAI I would expect that to be called out somewhere)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 5) The spell with the highest Arcanum is the base spell and that is the ruling Arcanum and the primary spell factor. If a tie for the highest then a coin flip, ST chooses, Player chooses?<br /> <br /> This also brings up another question. I would assume that you would still pay the Mana for any spell that was not in a Ruling Arcanum, Rote or Praxis, that was included in the combination spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T03:05:16-08:00","id":1028476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027744-the-mechanics-of-a-combination-spell?p=1028475#post1028475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 5) The spell with the highest Arcanum is the base spell and that is the ruling Arcanum and the primary spell factor. If a tie for the highest then a coin flip, ST chooses, Player chooses?<br /> <br /> This also brings up another question. I would assume that you would still pay the Mana for any spell that was not in a Ruling Arcanum, Rote or Praxis, that was included in the combination spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume so, but it's not explicitly stated one way or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T04:43:36-08:00","id":1028498,"title":"","content":"When you calculate Reach for the spell you take the lowest. When you calculate Potency and Duration, you also take the lowest. However, if a Reach is used to change Primary Factor on the spell(s) so that all combined spells have the same Primary Factor, you do get a number of free steps equal to the lowest Arcanum used in the spell. That's how I'd run it.<br /> I don't think it's a big deal since spells with Potency as the Primary Factor are most often never used with increased Duration because their effect is instant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T05:10:53-08:00","id":1028508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027744-the-mechanics-of-a-combination-spell?p=1028498#post1028498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you calculate Reach for the spell you take the lowest. When you calculate Potency and Duration, you also take the lowest. However, if a Reach is used to change Primary Factor on the spell(s) so that all combined spells have the same Primary Factor, you do get a number of free steps equal to the lowest Arcanum used in the spell. That's how I'd run it.<br /> I don't think it's a big deal since spells with Potency as the Primary Factor are most often never used with increased Duration because their effect is instant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking the lowest of Potency/Duration requires calculating them independently for each component, which seems pretty strongly against what the text implies happens. All spell factors are calculated together from my reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T05:24:32-08:00","id":1028510,"title":"","content":"I still think it's the best way to handle it since the book is very explicit about that changing primary spell factor requires a Reach.<br /> Combi-casting spells should not make the individual spells potentially more powerful because they in practice gain a free Reach or free spell factor steps.<br /> <br /> I really do love Mage, but the Combined Spell rules are a complete mess. I really hope <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> can clear it up either here or in the upcoming FAQ/errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-08-2017, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T06:37:31-08:00","id":1028525,"title":"","content":"I feel like the best bet for Primary Factor is just to take a cue from the Creative Thaumaturgy guidelines with regard to the combined effect, given that that's how the primary means of offsetting normal spell factor additions works as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T06:50:44-08:00","id":1028527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw page 125</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you start designing a spell that deals damage and grants bonus dice and imposes a Condition, you\u2019re probably creating a <span style=\"color:blue\">combined spell (see p. 118), not a single spell.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately this is all my book says in the Creative Thaumaturgy section about combining spells. Not real helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T07:08:53-08:00","id":1028532,"title":"","content":"I think Satchel means is if the spell were to be a single spell instead of a combined spell you'd determine the primary factor from that spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T07:23:12-08:00","id":1028536,"title":"","content":"But all of the spells already have a predefined Primary Spell Factor so it doesn't help when trying to figure out which one to use. I suppose that you could look at the desired result of the combination and see which Primary Spell Factor is in dominance for the final product. But then that would be more of a call on the ST's part to say that it it one or the other. So it would be ST's choice, but then he would adjudicate the end result anyway and if he felt that it was wrong he could change it anyway so may as well leave it as the players choice wit ST's approval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-08-2017, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T10:30:17-08:00","id":1028605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027744-the-mechanics-of-a-combination-spell?p=1028508#post1028508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking the lowest of Potency/Duration requires calculating them independently for each component, which seems pretty strongly against what the text implies happens. All spell factors are calculated together from my reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I went with the reading that I did because I'm comfortable with the extra bookkeeping it entails. If you insist on &quot;calculating the spell factors together&quot;, I'd rather rule that you use the lowest possible spell factor by default than making it so that every time someone casts Earthquake, they combine it with Receiver for 6 free dice, to take the extreme example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T11:02:53-08:00","id":1028609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027744-the-mechanics-of-a-combination-spell?p=1028605#post1028605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I went with the reading that I did because I'm comfortable with the extra bookkeeping it entails. If you insist on &amp;quot;calculating the spell factors together&amp;quot;, I'd rather rule that you use the lowest possible spell factor by default than making it so that every time someone casts Earthquake, they combine it with Receiver for 6 free dice, to take the extreme example.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't how that works. If you cast Receiver and Earthquake separately they would be using the same dice pool, if you cast them combined they have the same dice pool. I have no idea how you came to the conclusion that bonus dice are being handed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T12:46:30-08:00","id":1028656,"title":"","content":"It's less bonus dice being handed out and more saving dice for not having to spend them on upping the Duration because Receiver has Duration as its Primary Factor. You'd save 8 dice, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:26:41-08:00","id":1028786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027744-the-mechanics-of-a-combination-spell?p=1028609#post1028609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That isn't how that works. If you cast Receiver and Earthquake separately they would be using the same dice pool, if you cast them combined they have the same dice pool. I have no idea how you came to the conclusion that bonus dice are being handed out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using the rules interpretation wherein different primary spell factors in a combined spell means that you get Arcanum-1 steps for free in <i>all</i> primary spell factors, and assuming Gnosis 5, Forces 5,<br /> <br /> Earthquake at Duration 5 (4 steps) would be Gnosis 5 + Forces 5 - 8 (Duration) = 2 dice.<br /> Earthquake+Receiver at Duration 5 (0 steps) would be Gnosis 5 + Forces 5 - 2 (Combined Spell) = 8 dice.<br /> <br /> Difference of 6 dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}